<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="Perdido-C-Theme" spTempo="142">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1941 (music; lyrics added in 1944)
Composer:	Juan Tizol
Lyricist:	Ervin Drake and Hans Jan Lengsfelder
Form:	32-bar AABA
Style:	Swing
Key:	Bb major

Tizol wrote “Perdido” as an instrumental, and Duke Ellington’s
orchestra first recorded it in December 1941; Drake and
Lengsfelder added lyrics in 1944. The title refers to Perdido
Street in New Orleans, and the tune became a popular vehicle
for jazz solos and jam sessions.</spComments>
